suffix.-ник:
===Etymology===
{{etymon|ru|:inh|sla-pro:*-ьnikъ}}
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*-ьnikъ}}, itself originally by [[nominalization]] of adjectives in {{m|sla-pro|*-ьnъ}} with the suffix {{m|sla-pro|*-ikъ}} (whence {{m|ru|-ик}}). The suffix originates from the {{der|ru|ine-bsl-pro|-}} period; compare dialectal Lithuanian {{m|lt|laukinykas|lauk-inykas|peasant, farmer}} (from {{m|lt|laukas|laũkas|field}}) and Old Prussian {{m|prg|laukinikis|lauk-inikis|vassal}}.

===Suffix===
{{head|ru|suffix|head=-ник|head2=-ни́к|cat2=noun-forming suffixes}}

# Suffix appended to nominal stems to create a masculine noun, usually denoting a professional, performer, adherent, place, object, tool or a feature.
#: {{sufex|ru|лы́жа|t1=[[ski]]|лы́жник|t2=[[skier]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|путь|t1=[[way]], [[path]], [[road]]|пу́тник|t2=[[traveler]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|бюдже́т|t1=[[budget]]|бюдже́тник|t2=[[government]] [[employee]]|qq2=colloquial}}
#: {{sufex|ru|кни́га|t1=[[book]]|кни́жник|t2=[[bookseller]]; [[book]] [[lover]]; [[scribe]]|qq2=colloquial}}
#: {{sufex|ru|двор|t1=[[yard]], [[courtyard]]|дво́рник|t2=[[janitor]]; [[street]] [[cleaner]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|бума́га|t1=[[paper]], [[document]]|бума́жник|t2=[[wallet]]; [[papermaker]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|пар|t1=[[vapor]]|парни́к|t2=[[greenhouse]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|учёба|t1=[[studies]], [[learning]]|уче́бник|t2=[[textbook]]; [[manual]]}}

====Usage notes====
The suffix has the same properties as {{m|ru|-ный}}:
* A velar (as well as {{lang|ru|ц}}) normally turns into a palatal as a result of the {{glossary|Slavic first palatalization}}.
*: {{m|ru|сапо́г|t=[[shoe]]}} → {{m|ru|сапо́жник|t=[[cobbler]]}}
*: {{m|ru|скворе́ц|t=[[starling]]}} → {{m|ru|скворе́чник|t=[[birdhouse]], [[nestbox]]|tr=skvoréšnik, skvoréčnik}}
* A stem ending in {{lang|ru|-л}} turns into {{lang|ru|-ль}} before the suffix; contrariwise, all other stems ending in {{lang|ru|-ь}} lose this.
*: {{m|ru|шко́ла|t=[[school]]}} → {{m|ru|шко́льник|t=[[schoolboy]]}}
*: {{m|ru|ла́герь|t=[[camp]]}} → {{m|ru|ла́герник|t=[[prisoner]] (in a [[labor camp]] or [[concentration camp]])}}
* With reducible nouns, the stem assumes its non-reduced form before the suffix. With feminine and neuter nouns, this form is found only in the genitive plural. This applies even to nouns with no plural.
*: {{m|ru|яйцо́|t=[[egg]]}}, genitive plural {{m|ru|яи́ц}} → {{m|ru|яи́чник|t=[[ovary]]|tr=jaíšnik, jaíčnik}}
*: {{m|ru|се́рдце|t=[[heart]]}}, genitive plural {{m|ru|серде́ц}} → {{m|ru|серде́чник|t=[[core]], [[inner]] [[part]] of a [[machine]]}}
*: {{m|ru|ядро́|t=[[nucleus]]}}, genitive plural {{m|ru|я́дер}} → {{m|ru|я́дерник|t=[[nuclear]] [[physicist]]}}
*: {{m|ru|ружьё|t=[[gun]]}}, genitive plural {{m|ru||ру́жей}} → {{m|ru|руже́йник|t=[[gunsmith]]}}
* {{lang|ru|ё}} may turn back into {{lang|ru|е}} before the suffix.
*: {{m|ru|лёд|t=[[ice]]}} → {{m|ru|ледни́к|t=[[icehouse]], [[icebox]]}}
* The stress is sometimes (but not always) drawn onto the preceding syllable.
*: {{m|ru|ружьё|t=[[gun]]}}, genitive plural {{m|ru||ру́жей}} → {{m|ru|руже́йник|t=[[gunsmith]]}}
* Foreign nouns ending in invariant {{lang|ru|-е}} change this to stressed {{lang|ru|-е́й}} before the suffix.
*: {{m|ru|ко́фе|t=[[coffee]]}} → {{m|ru|кофе́йник|t=[[coffee pot]]}}
*: {{m|ru|шоссе́|tr=šossɛ́|t=[[highway]]}} → {{m|ru|шоссе́йник|tr=šossɛ́jnik|t=[[racing]] [[bicycle]], [[racing]] [[cyclist]]}}
* Some adjectives in {{lang|ru|-ия}}, {{lang|ru|-ие}} change this to stressed {{lang|ru|-е́й}} before the suffix (as if they ended in {{lang|ru|-ья}}, {{lang|ru|-ье}}/{{lang|ru|-ьё}}).
*: {{m|ru|ору́жие|t=[[weapon]], [[arms]]}} → {{m|ru|оруже́йник|t=[[weapon]]s [[maker]], [[armorer]], [[gunsmith]]}}

Additional properties:
* Nouns in {{lang|ru|-ник}} may be formed directly from adjectives in {{m|ru|-ный}} when no base noun exists or has a different meaning:
*: {{m|ru|поля́рный||[[polar]]}} (formed from a foreign word, e.g. {{cog|de|polar}}) → {{m|ru|поля́рник|t=[[polar]] [[explorer]]}}
*: {{m|ru|ча́стный||[[private]]}} (formed from {{m|ru|часть||[[part]], [[share]]}}) → {{m|ru|ча́стник|t={{q|colloquial}} [[private]] [[owner]], [[private]] [[entrepreneur]]}}
* Not all nouns ending in {{lang|ru|-ник}} contain this suffix. Some contain {{lang|ru|-ик}}, e.g. {{m|ru|чле́ник||{{q|anatomy}} [[segment]]}} from {{m|ru|член||[[limb]]}}.
* In some nouns, the suffix is stressed, in which case it declines according to accent pattern b (always end-stressed).
*: {{m|ru|ледни́к||[[glacier]]}}, genitive singular {{m|ru|ледника́}}, nominative plural {{m|ru|ледники́}}

Note in particular that nouns in {{m|ru|-ка}}, {{m|ru|-ко}} have corresponding derived nouns in unstressed {{lang|ru|-очник}} or {{lang|ru|-ечник}}.

