suffix.-ка:
===Etymology 1===
Inherited from Proto-Slavic [[Reconstruction:Proto-Slavic/-ka|*-ka]].<ref>{{cite-book|last=Фасмер|first=Макс|title=Этимологический словарь русского языка. Том II (Е – Муж)|translator=О. Н. Трубачев|location=Москва|year=1986|publisher=Прогресс|entry=ка, -ко|page=147}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:LIPP|vol=1|page=429|entry=2.*ko}}</ref>

====Particle====
{{head|ru|particle}}

# [[just]], ([[now]]) [[would]] [[you]]? {{qualifier|appended to an imperative verb to soften the command somewhat}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[дай|Да́й]]'''-ка''' [[пройти|пройду́]]|If you'''’ll just''' step aside…}}
# [[now]], ([[real quick|real]]) [[quick]], [[just]] {{qualifier|appended to an imperative verb to express urgency or a pressing request}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[идти|Иди́те]]'''-ка''' [[сюда́]]|'''Just''' come here!}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[послушать|Послу́шай]]'''-ка''', [[па́рень]]|'''Now''' listen, lad!}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|crp-slb|-ка}}
* {{desc|izh|-k|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymon|ru|id=nominal|:blend|orv:-ъка<ety:inh<sla-pro:*-ъka>>|orv:-ька<ety:inh<sla-pro:*-ьka<ety:der<ine-bsl-pro:*-kāˀ<id:suffix><ety:inh<ine-pro:*-kos<alt:*-keh₂><id:adjectives>>>>>>>|tree=1}}
From a conflation of two suffixes {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*-ьka}} and {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*-ъka}}. The former always came to be used after velars (hence the occurrence of the {{lg|Slavic first palatalization}}), while the latter always came to be used after -л- (hence the lack of palatalization of -л- before -ка).

====Suffix====
{{head|ru|suffix}}

# {{n-g|(added to (normally feminine) nouns, forms diminutives, sometimes with a further change in meaning)}}
#: {{sufex|ru|жи́ла|t1=[[vein]]|жи́лка|t2=[[veinlet]], [[small]] [[vein]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|моги́ла|t1=[[grave]]|моги́лка|t2=[[small]] [[grave]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|бума́га|t1=[[paper]], [[document]]|бума́жка|t2=[[small]] [[document]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|ку́кла|t1=[[doll]], [[puppet]]|qq1=genitive plural {{m|ru|ку́кол}}|ку́колка|t2=[[small]] [[doll]], [[pupa]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|пчела́|t1=[[bee]]|пчёлка|t2=[[small]] [[bee]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|вода́|t1=[[water]]|во́дка|t2=[[vodka]]|qq2=originally, "something [[dilute]]d with [[water]]"}}
# {{n-g|(added to nouns denoting classes of people, forms the feminine equivalent; replaces the suffix {{m|ru|-ец}} if present)}}
#: {{sufex|ru|ленингра́дец|t1=resident of [[Leningrad]]|ленингра́дка|t2=[[female]] [[resident]] of [[Leningrad]]}}
# {{n-g|(added to verbs, forms abstract nouns or nouns indicating the result of the action)}}
#: {{sufex|ru|закали́ть|t1=to [[temper]], to [[harden]]|зака́лка|t2=[[temper]]ing, [[harden]]ing; [[training]] {{q|for [[endurance]]}}}}
#: {{sufex|ru|мочи́ть|t1=to [[soak]], to [[wet]]|мо́чка|t2=[[soak]]ing, [[wet]]ting}}
#: {{sufex|ru|отде́лать|t1=to [[finish]], to [[trim]]|отде́лка|t2=[[finish]]ing, [[trim]]ming; [[finish]], [[trim]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|подде́лать|t1=to [[counterfeit]], to [[fake]]|подде́лка|t2=[[counterfeit]], [[imitation]], [[fake]], [[forgery]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|блоки́ровать|t1=to [[block]]|блокиро́вка|t2=[[block]]ing, [[blockage]]}}
# {{n-g|(added to verbs, forms instruments or tools)}}
#: {{sufex|ru|заколо́ть|t1=to [[attach]] with a [[pin]]|зако́лка|t2=[[barrette]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|пили́ть|t1=to [[saw]]|пи́лка|t2=[[fretsaw]]; [[fingernail]] [[file]]}}
# {{n-g|(added to adjectives or numerals, forms colloquial nouns with the meaning of a carrier of the adjective's or numeral's properties)}}
#: {{sufex|ru|минера́льный|t1=[[mineral]] {{q|relational}}|минера́лка|t2=[[mineral water]] {{q|colloquial}}; [[mineral]] [[fertilizer]] {{q|colloquial}}}}
#: {{sufex|ru|зени́тный|t1=[[zenith]] {{q|relational}}; [[anti-aircraft]] {{q|relational}}|зени́тка|t2=[[anti-aircraft]] [[gun]] {{q|colloquial}}}}
#: {{sufex|ru|полтора́|t1=[[one and a half]]|qq1=oblique cases {{m|ru|полу́тора}}|полу́торка|t2=[[small]] [[apartment]] [[consisting]] of a [[medium]]-[[size]]d [[room]] and a [[small]] [[room]] {{q|colloquial}}; GAZ-AA-brand [[truck]] with a 1.5-[[ton]] [[payload]] {{q|colloquial}}}}
#: {{sufex|ru|запрещённый|t1=[[forbidden]]|запрещёнка|t2=[[something]] forbidden {{q|colloquial}}}}

=====Usage notes=====
* When {{m|ru||-ка}} is appended to someone's name (e.g. "Ava-shka"), it acts as a diminuitive, and shows endearment. 

Note the following properties:
* If the stress is on the ending, it is drawn onto the preceding syllable. Unstressed е may turn into ё when stressed.
*: {{sufex|ru|вода́|t1=[[water]]|во́дка|t2=[[vodka]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|бечева́|t1=[[twine]]|бечёвка|t2=[[twine]]}} (originally, "small twine")
* If the stress is not on the ending, it generally remains in the same place, but when added onto verbs ending in {{m|ru|-и́ровать}}, the stress moves onto {{lang|ru|-ов-}}.
*: {{sufex|ru|блоки́ровать|t1=to [[block]]|блокиро́вка|t2=[[block]]ing, [[blockage]]}}
* A velar may turn into a palatal as a result of the {{glossary|Slavic first palatalization}}. This is due to the {{lang|ru|*ь}} that was formerly present at the beginning of one variant of the suffix.
*: {{sufex|ru|апте́ка|t1=[[pharmacy]]|апте́чка|t2=[[medicine]] [[box]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|бума́га|t1=[[paper]]|бума́жка|t2=[[small]] [[document]]}}
* If the noun is feminine or neuter and reducible, the unreduced stem (as found in the genitive plural) is used. This happens frequently when the suffix is added onto a noun already in diminutive form.
*: {{sufex|ru|ку́кла|t1=[[doll]], [[puppet]]|qq1=genitive plural {{m|ru|ку́кол}}|ку́колка|t2=[[small]] [[doll]], [[pupa]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|бу́дка|t1=[[booth]]|qq1=genitive plural {{m|ru|бу́док}}|бу́дочка|t2=small [[booth]]}}

