====Usage notes====
* The diminutive suffix is always unstressed and normally does not trigger any change in the stress, although in some cases the stress is drawn onto the preceding syllable (e.g., {{m|ru|воло́сик}} from {{m|ru|во́лос}}).
* The agent-noun suffix is often stressed.
* When added onto a noun ending in {{lang|ru|ц}}, the suffix triggers the {{glossary|Slavic first palatalization}}, resulting in {{lang|ru|ч}}. The same would be expected to happen to the velars {{lang|ru|к}}, {{lang|ru|г}}{{,}} and {{lang|ru|х}}, but there appear to be no examples of this.
* When added onto a {{glossary|reducible}} noun, the stem assumes its reduced form before the suffix (e.g., {{m|ru|за́йчик}} from {{m|ru|за́яц}}).

