suffix.-ный:
===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ru|-но́й||when the ending is stressed}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|ru|:bor|cu:-ьнъ<alt:-ьныи>}}
{{bor+|ru|cu|-ьнъ|-ьныи}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*-ьnъ|*-ьnъjь}}. {{doublet|ru|-ной}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ru|suffix|cat2=adjective-forming suffixes|soft variant|-ний}}

# [[-ish]], [[-ic]], [[-al]], [[-ed]]; {{non-gloss|having a particular quality of, pertaining to, associated with; forms adjectives from nouns, and sometimes from verbs}}
#: {{sufex|ru|культу́ра|t1=[[culture]]|культу́рный|t2=[[cultural]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|ме́сто|t1=[[place]]|ме́стный|t2=[[local]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|наро́д|t1=[[people]]|наро́дный|t2=[[folk]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|не́га|t1=[[comfort]]|не́жный|t2=[[gentle]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|нормати́в|t1=[[norm]]|нормати́вный|t2=[[normative]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|свобо́да|t1=[[freedom]]|свобо́дный|t2=[[free]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|учёба|t1=[[studies]], [[training]]|уче́бный|t2=[[educational]], {{q|relational}} [[training]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|се́рия|t1=[[series]]|сери́йный|t2=[[serial]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|грех|t1=[[sin]]|гре́шный|t2=[[sinful]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|не-|обы́чай|t2=[[custom]]|необыча́йный|t3=[[unusual]], [[extraordinary]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|molekular|lang1=de|молекуля́рный|t2=[[molecular]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|Kassation|lang1=de|кассацио́нный|t2={{q|relational}} [[appeal]], [[cassation]]}}
#: {{sufex|ru|томи́ть|t1=to [[tire]], to [[exhaust]]|то́мный|t2=[[languid]], [[languorous]]}}

====Usage notes====
Note the following properties:
* A velar (as well as {{lang|ru|ц}}) normally turns into a palatal as a result of the {{glossary|Slavic first palatalization}}. This and the following several properties are due to the {{lang|ru|*ь}} that was formerly present at the beginning of the suffix.
*: {{sufex|ru|не́га|t1=[[comfort]]|не́жный|t2=[[gentle]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|грех|t1=[[sin]]|гре́шный|t2=[[sinful]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|се́рдце|t1=[[heart]]|qq1=genitive plural {{m|ru|серде́ц}}|серде́чный|t2=[[cordial]]}}
* A stem ending in {{lang|ru|-л}} turns into {{lang|ru|-ль}} before the suffix; contrariwise, all other stems ending in {{lang|ru|-ь}} lose this.
*: {{sufex|ru|глаго́л|t1=[[verb]]|глаго́льный|t2=[[verbal]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|ла́герь|t1=[[camp]]|ла́герный|t2={{q|relational}} [[camp]]}}
* With reducible nouns, the stem assumes its non-reduced form before the suffix. With feminine and neuter nouns, this form is found only in the genitive plural. This applies even to nouns with no plural.
*: {{sufex|ru|земля́|t1=[[land]]|qq1=genitive plural {{m|ru|земе́ль}}|земе́льный|t2={{q|relational}} [[land]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|ядро́|t1=[[nucleus]]|qq1=genitive plural {{m|ru|я́дер}}|я́дерный|t2=[[nuclear]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|ёлка|t1=[[Christmas tree]]|qq1=genitive plural {{m|ru|ёлок}}|ёлочный|t2={{q|relational}} [[Christmas tree]]}} {{q|к is palatalized in accordance with a preceding property}}
*: {{sufex|ru|во́дка|t1=[[vodka]]|qq1=genitive plural {{m|ru||*во́док}}|во́дочный|t2={{q|relational}} [[vodka]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|литьё|t1=[[casting]]|qq1=genitive plural {{m|ru||*лите́й}}|лите́йный|t2={{q|relational}} [[casting]]}}
* {{lang|ru|ё}} may turn back into {{lang|ru|е}} before the suffix.
*: {{sufex|ru|учёба|t1=[[studies]], [[training]]|уче́бный|t2=[[educational]], {{q|relational}} [[training]]}}, but
*: {{sufex|ru|учёт|t1=[[registration]]|учётный|t2={{q|relational}} [[registration]]}}
* The stress is sometimes (but not always) drawn onto the preceding syllable.
*: {{af|ru|не-|t1=un-|обы́чай|t2=[[custom]]|nocat=1}} → {{m|ru|необыча́йный|t=[[unusual]], [[extraordinary]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|се́рия|t1=[[series]]|сери́йный|t2=[[serial]]}}
* Foreign nouns ending in invariant {{lang|ru|-е}} change this to stressed {{lang|ru|-е́й}} before the suffix.
*: {{sufex|ru|ко́фе|t1=[[coffee]]|кофе́йный|t2={{q|relational}} [[coffee]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|шоссе́|tr1=šossɛ́|t1=[[highway]]|шоссе́йный|tr2=šossɛ́jnyj|t2={{q|relational}} [[highway]]}}
* Some adjectives in {{lang|ru|-ия}}, {{lang|ru|-ие}} change this to stressed {{lang|ru|-е́й}} before the suffix (as if they ended in {{lang|ru|-ья}}, {{lang|ru|-ье}}/{{lang|ru|-ьё}}).
*: {{sufex|ru|ору́жие|t1=[[weapon]], [[arms]]|оруже́йный|t2={{q|relational}} [[weapon]], [[gun]], [[arms]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|ли́ния|t1=[[line]]|лине́йный|t2=[[linear]]}}
* But some adjectives in {{lang|ru|-ия}}, {{lang|ru|-ие}} have the expected change to {{lang|ru|-и́й}}:
*: {{sufex|ru|ору́дие|t1=[[large]] [[gun]]|оруди́йный|t2={{q|relational}} [[large]] [[gun]]}}
*: {{sufex|ru|се́рия|t1=[[series]]|сери́йный|t2=[[serial]]}}
* Adjectives in {{lang|ru|-ный}} may be formed directly from foreign nouns or adjectives, as in {{m|ru|молекуля́рный|t=[[molecular]]}} and {{m|ru|кассацио́нный|t={{q|relational}} [[appeal]], [[cassation]]}} (there is no such adjective {{lang|ru|*молекуля́р}} and no such noun {{lang|ru|*кассацио́н}}). In particular, nouns ending in -ия (from Latin -io with oblique stem -ion) form adjectives ending in -ио́нный (see {{m|ru|-онный}}): {{sufex|ru|пози́ция|t1=[[position]]|позицио́нный|t2=[[positional]]}}. Sometimes this pattern is extended to nouns ending in -ия which come from Latin -ia, as in {{sufex|ru|интерфере́нция|t1=[[interference]]|интерференцио́нный|t2={{q|relational}} [[interference]]}}.

Note in particular that nouns in {{m|ru|-ка}}, {{m|ru|-ко}} have corresponding adjectives in unstressed {{lang|ru|-очный}}.

