# {{n-g|Used to form imperfective verbs from prefixed perfective verbs. Normally used with stems ending in paired non-palatal consonants, but occasionally found with stems ending in paired palatal consonants, with the consonant becoming non-palatal before this suffix.}}
#: {{m|ru|отде́лать|g=pf}} → {{m|ru|отде́лывать|g=impf}}
#: {{m|ru|записа́ть|g=pf}} → {{m|ru|запи́сывать|g=impf}}
#: {{m|ru|срабо́тать|g=pf}} → {{m|ru|сраба́тывать|g=impf}}
#: {{m|ru|опроки́нуть|g=pf}} → {{m|ru|опроки́дывать|g=impf}}
#: {{m|ru|обхвати́ть|g=pf}} → {{m|ru|обхва́тывать|g=impf}}
#: {{m|ru|заката́ть|g=pf}} → {{m|ru|зака́тывать|g=impf}}
# {{n-g|Used to form [[frequentative]] verbs from non-prefixed imperfective verbs.}}
#: {{sufex|ru|писа́ть|t1=to write|пи́сывать|t2=to write repeatedly}}
#: {{sufex|ru|чита́ть|t1=to read|чи́тывать|t2=to read repeatedly}}

====Usage notes====
The frequentative and imperfectivizing suffixes are etymologically the same. The suffixes are used with verbs in {{m|ru|-ать}} and {{m|ru|-нуть}} (in the latter case, the underlying root reappears, which may involve an extra consonant that was lost before the -н- of the verbal suffix). They are also used with some verbs in {{m|ru|-ить}}. The spelling variant {{m|ru|-ивать}} is used instead with verbs that end in root-final velars ({{lang|ru|к г х}}) and hushing consonants ({{lang|ru|ш ж ч щ}}). The stress is drawn onto the syllable before the suffix, and an {{lang|ru|о}} in that syllable usually changes into {{lang|ru|а}} (examples: {{m|ru|замора́живать|g=impf}}, {{m|ru|отмора́живать|g=impf}}, {{m|ru|выздора́вливать|g=impf}}; exception: {{m|ru|застрахо́вывать|g=impf}}).

