suffix.-нуть:
===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*-nǫti}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|-нуть|ann=y}}
* {{ru-IPA|-ну́ть|ann=y}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ru|suffix|head=-нуть|head2=-ну́ть|cat2=verb-forming suffixes}}

# {{n-g|suffix used to create primary {{glossary|imperfective}} {{glossary|intransitive}} verbs}}
# {{n-g|suffix used to create derived {{glossary|perfective}} verbs, most of which are {{glossary|semelfactive}}}}

====Usage notes====
* There are two related verbal suffixes. One variant suffix forms primary verbs (i.e. verbs formed directly from a root), and the other variant forms secondary verbs (i.e. verbs originally derived from other terms, although this may no be longer be obvious), usually with a {{glossary|semelfactive}} meaning, i.e. with the meaning "to do something once". The properties and conjugations of the two variants are distinct:
** The primary (type-1) suffix is always unstressed. It forms verbs that are imperfective when unprefixed (perfective when prefixed, as usual), and are usually {{glossary|intransitive}}. The {{lang|ru|-н}} of the suffix tends to disappear in the past tense. Examples:
*** {{m|ru|ги́бнуть||to [[die]], to [[perish]]}}
*** {{m|ru|мёрзнуть||to [[freeze]]}}
*** {{m|ru|блёкнуть||to [[fade]], to [[pale]]}}
*** {{m|ru|ли́пнуть||to [[stick]]}}
*** {{m|ru|сты́нуть||to [[wither]], to [[cool down]]}}
*** {{m|ru|-ве́ргнуть||to [[throw]]}} (only prefixed)
** The secondary (type-2) suffix may be stressed or unstressed. It forms {{glossary|intransitive}} and {{glossary|transitive}} verbs, which are {{glossary|perfective}} when unprefixed. The {{lang|ru|-н}} of the suffix is present in all tenses. Examples:
*** {{m|ru|дви́нуть||to [[move]] (something)}}
*** {{m|ru|тяну́ть||to [[pull]]}}
*** {{m|ru|хлебну́ть||to [[swallow]] a [[mouthful]] of (something)}}
* Note, for example, the following contrasts:
{|class="wikitable"
! type 1 !! past masc !! past fem !! type 2 !! past masc !! past fem
|-
| imperfective {{m|ru|дро́гнуть||to [[freeze]], to [[feel]] [[cold]]}} || {{m|ru|дрог}}/{{m|ru|дро́гнул}} || {{m|ru|дро́гла}} || perfective {{m|ru|дро́гнуть||to [[shiver]], to [[shake]]}} || {{m|ru|дро́гнул}} || {{m|ru|дро́гнула}}
|-
| imperfective {{m|ru|па́хнуть||to [[smell]] (of), to [[have]] a [[smell]]}} || {{m|ru|пах}}/{{m|ru|па́хнул}} || {{m|ru|па́хла}} || perfective {{m|ru|пахну́ть||to [[puff]], to [[blow]]}} || {{m|ru|пахну́л}} || {{m|ru|пахну́ла}}
|-
| prefixed perfective {{m|ru|промо́кнуть||to [[get]] [[wet]], to [[get]] [[soak]]ed}} || {{m|ru|промо́к}} || {{m|ru|промо́кла}} || prefixed perfective {{m|ru|промокну́ть||to [[blot]] ([[paper]])}} || {{m|ru|промокну́л}} || {{m|ru|промокну́ла}}
|}

====Conjugation====
