===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|-сь}} {{qualifier|after vowels}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|ru|:inh|orv:сѧ|tree=+}}
From {{inh|ru|orv|сѧ}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*sę}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*sen}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*swé}}. It is considered the shortened form of {{m|ru|себя́}}. Compare {{cog|be|-}} and {{cog|uk|-ся}}, {{cog|it|-si}}, {{cog|es|se}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|-ся}}
* {{ru-IPA|-са}} {{qualifier|after {{lang|ru|т}} or {{lang|ru|ть}}|see usage notes}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Lvova--ся.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ru|suffix}}

# {{n-g|Reflexive suffix appended to finite verbs and infinitives to make a [[reflexive]], [[reciprocal]], [[intransitive]] or [[passive]] verb.}}

====Usage notes====
* After a vowel, {{lang|ru|'''-ся'''}} is usually contracted to {{lang|ru|'''-сь'''}}, except when attached to an adjectival participle:
** {{l|ru|мы́ться||to wash oneself}}, {{l|ru||мо́ется|[he] washes himself}}
** {{l|ru|мыться|мо́юсь|[I] wash myself}}
** {{l|ru|мывшийся|мы́вшаяся|having been washing herself}}.
* When affixed to an infinitive {{l|ru|-ть}} or the 3rd-person singular or plural {{l|ru|-т}}, it merges with the /tʲ/ or /t/ into the affricate /ts/ and palatalization is lost: {{IPAchar|[tsə]}}.

